arXiv:2611.13598v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: For Schwartz functions $f_1,f_2$ on $\mathbb{R}$, define the bilinear Hilbert transform by $$
  \mathbf{BHT}(f_1,f_2)(x)
  =\operatorname{p.v.}\int_{\mathbb{R}}
  f_1(x-t)f_2(x+t)\,\frac{dt}{t}. $$ We prove the weak-type estimate $$
  \left\|\mathbf{BHT}(f_1,f_2)\right\|_{L^{2/3,\infty}}
  \lesssim_{p_1,p_2}
  \|f_1\|_{p_1}\|f_2\|_{p_2} $$ for $1<p_1,p_2<2$ with $1/p_1+1/p_2=3/2$. The key ingredient is a new local supremum estimate for packet sums, which we use to establish the forest estimate.

arXiv:2611.11942v2 Announce Type: replace Abstract: Let $\Gamma=\{1,\dots,d\}$, $d\geq 2$. For each $j\in \Gamma$, let ${\ell}_{j}\geq 1$ be an integer and let $\alpha_{j}\in (1/2,1)$. We obtain a pointwise estimate for the integral  egin{equation*} \int_{\mathbb{S}^{d-1}}\prod_{j\in \Gamma} |x^{\ell_{j}}_{j}-\xi_{j}|^{-\alpha_{j}} d \sigma(x), \end{equation*} in the region  egin{equation*} \{\xi\in \mathbb{R}^{d}: \xi_{j}
eq 0,\;j\in\Gamma,\;\; \sum
olimits_{j\in F}|\xi_{j}|^{2/\ell_{j}}
eq 1,\; F\subseteq \Gamma\}. \end{equation*} These estimates are used to prove a Tomas - Stein type restriction theorem for the oscillatory integral operator $Tf(x)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^d}e^{\dot{\imath}h(x,y)}f(y)dy$, with the phase $h(x,y)=\sum
olimits_{j\in\Gamma} a_{j} x_{j}^{\ell_{j}} y_{j}^{m_{j}}$, where, for each $j\in \Gamma$, $a_{j}
eq 0$ is a real number and $m_{j}>1$ is an integer.
